cally explain away  the lack of shika towers and pillars  seen in the trailer  but the divine beasts are a bit  different since they have  you know legs and stuff we don't have  much reason to believe that they would  bury themselves underground  so perhaps they were moved by something  instead could it be possible that the  princess  upon retaking the throne of hyrule and  rallying the hylians back to a unified  civilization  formulated a research team and slowly  but surely dismantled or just  moved the divine beasts for the purpose  of her research  that does seem in line with what zelda  was all about prior to the great  calamity  and with ganon's return being classified  as something that will always come back  given the passage of time it makes sense  that she'd still want to understand how  the shika weapons work  so she can render them useful for future  generations  very well put i think that wraps up the  missing chica tech very nicely now let's  talk about the missing pieces of nature  like the lava on death mountain or the  missing deku tree  as far as death mountain no longer  producing lava is concerned  that could simply be due to link having  calmed vardanya in the first game which  may have led to the volcano calming down  long enough to the point to where the  air is livable around it  like most of the dormant volcanoes in  our own real life world  as for the deku tree though the fact  that it's missing is very interesting  indeed  see we already went over how we know  this hyrule is present  future day hyrule and not the hyrule of  the past meaning it's not probable that  this is simply before the deku tree  sprouted fully  that means something moved it again  unless the draw distance is just really  really bad in the sequel as nintendo  black crisis mentioned in his analysis  video  ganondorf has a history of attacking the  deku tree actually in ocarina of time he  kills the deku tree since he's  apparently free now in breath of the  wild sequel  and since the deku tree now plays a  larger role than ever in guarding the  master sword itself as nintendo black  crisis stated ganondorf has  every reason to go after it but as he  also mentions it could also be missing  due to having risen into skyloft  possibly to escape from ganondorf's  attacks since we can't see very  clearly in that direction in the trailer  there's no way of telling whether it's  just the deku tree missing and the rest  of the korok forest is there or there's  now just a giant crater in the ground  where it all used to be but no matter  what we speculate it's always centered  around ganondorf's revival and his  probable assault on the deku tree  the last thing we'll cover in this  differences explained video are the  strange blocky rocks that are sticking  out of the ground in this shot  now personally i am a huge fan of the  notion that they are fallen blocks or  pillars from skyrule above  i mean they're new to this game and  their blocky design resembles the  pillars present in this dungeon that  link is rapidly trying to fill with fire  and the islands of skyrim are also  filled with blocky designs for the  grounds and buildings  given that they were not present in the  first game and they mimic the designs of  all the weird skyrule stuff in the  trailer  i'd say saying these blocks here are  fallen from skyro is about as clear-cut  as speculation as we can get what do you  think mr crisis  yeah i think we just about covered it  all well awesome and hey man thanks  again for helping out with this one  there's just  so many possibilities with everything  we've been shown and it really helped  that you were here thanks for having me  on again  i have to say that i'm very excited for  this game  quick reminder that the collaboration  over on my channel will be uploaded in a  couple days  so stay tuned for that we'll be talking  about who may have been responsible for  the sky ruins  now if you'll excuse me i think i just  saw a zona  swirl outside best of luck with checking  that out there man i wonder what he's  gonna think when he replays wind waker  and realizes that there's a green zone i  swirl  present every time a dialog box is open  anyway huge thanks to everyone for  watching and a humongous thanks to my  amazing bandit crew who are the  reason that i can make these videos with  the amazing people that i make them with  if you watching are interested in  getting your name up here having a hand  in making these videos  and helping me buy chicken nuggies for  my tummies then please feel free to  click that join button below or follow  the links in my description for my  patreon and merch pages  also down there are the links to my  social media pages so come follow me on  instagram for some random nuggets of  happiness and geeky zelda stuff  or you know just whatever i feel like as  always i hope you have a wonderful rest  of your day  this is mass intended bandit signing out  and looking forward to seeing you in the  next one  [Music]  you
 

